6 0 obj
<< /Length 3969 >>
stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 729 Td (in pits or chambers that can flood. Use the LF-60P for flooded locations.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 704 Td (6. Pipe preparation) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 682 Td (Flush the line to remove debris before fitting the meter. Check that the mating flanges are EN) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 669 Td (1092-1 PN16, parallel within 0.5 mm, and that the bolt holes are aligned. The flange gap must) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 656 Td (equal the meter face-to-face length plus two gaskets: 200 mm for DN25 to DN50, 250 mm for DN65) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 643 Td (to DN100 and 300 mm for DN125 to DN200.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 618 Td (7. Mechanical installation and orientation) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 596 Td (The arrow on the meter body shows the forward flow direction. The preferred orientation is a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 583 Td (horizontal pipe with the electronics housing at the side \(3 o'clock or 9 o'clock\). Vertical) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 570 Td (pipe with upward flow is also acceptable. Do not install with the electronics housing directly) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 557 Td (underneath the pipe.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 535 Td (Use gaskets with an inside diameter no smaller than the pipe bore; a protruding gasket causes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 522 Td (L-204 low signal quality warnings. Compressed fibre gaskets are suitable across the full LF-60) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 509 Td (temperature range.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 484 Td (8. Electrical installation) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 462 Td (Use screened twisted-pair instrument cable of 0.5 to 1.5 mm\262. Close unused cable entries with) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 449 Td (the blanking plug to maintain IP65.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 428 Td (Terminal | Function | Notes) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 416 Td (1 | +24 VDC supply | 24 VDC \26110%, 4 W) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 404 Td (2 | 0 V supply |) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 392 Td (3 | 4-20 mA + | Active or passive, selected in menu) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 380 Td (4 | 4-20 mA - | No HART on the LF-60) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 368 Td (5 | Pulse output + | Open collector, max 30 VDC, 100 mA, max 1 kHz) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 356 Td (6 | Pulse output - |) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 344 Td (7 | RS-485 A \(D+\) | Modbus RTU) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 332 Td (8 | RS-485 B \(D-\) | Modbus RTU) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 320 Td (9 | Functional earth / screen |) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 298 Td (The RS-485 termination resistor is switched on with DIP switch S1. The LF-60 draws 4 W, around) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 285 Td (170 mA at 24 VDC, and starts measuring about 20 seconds after power is applied.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 260 Td (9. Grounding and bonding) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 238 Td (On bare metallic pipe, connect the grounding lug on each meter flange to the mating pipe flange) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 225 Td (with the supplied 6 mm\262 braided straps and connect terminal 9 to plant functional earth. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 212 Td (resistance between the meter body and plant earth must be less than 1 ohm.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 190 Td (On plastic or internally lined pipe, grounding rings are mandatory on both sides of the meter.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 177 Td (Use the 316L rings LF-GR-{size}-S \(for example LF-GR-050-S for DN50\). Grounding rings add 3 mm) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 164 Td (per side to the installed length.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 139 Td (10. Output configuration) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 117 Td (The LF-60 has no HART interface. Configure the 4-20 mA range under Menu > Setup > Outputs >) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 104 Td (Current > Range, where 20 mA corresponds to the upper range value in the selected flow unit.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 91 Td (The pulse output value \(litres per pulse\) is set under Menu > Setup > Outputs > Pulse > Pulse) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 78 Td (Value. Modbus settings are under Menu > Setup > Outputs > Modbus; the defaults are address 1,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 65 Td (9600 baud, 8N1. Use Menu > Diagnostics > Loop Test to force the current output to 4, 12 and 20) Tj ET
endstream
